<%- include("/partials/head", {
  title: "Subgrid Playground",
  description: "Line up the parts of cards and form fields with CSS subgrid.",
  appClass: "subgrid-playground",
  tour: true,
  styles: [
    "/shared/controls.css",
    "/shared/compat.css",
    "/shared/tour.css",
    "/shared/info.css",
    "/shared/grid.css",
    "/pages/subgrid/style.css",
  ],
  scripts: [
    "/shared/compat.js",
    "/shared/tour.js",
    "/shared/info.js",
    "/shared/frame.js",
    "/pages/subgrid/script.js",
  ],
}) %>
      <p class="app__intro">
        Cards in a row rarely have the same amount of content, so their titles, text and prices end up at different
        heights. <strong>Subgrid</strong> lets each card use its parent grid's rows (or columns) instead of making its
        own, so the parts <strong>line up</strong> across the row. Click any title or text to edit it and watch the row
        adjust.
      </p>

      <div class="controls">
        <%- include("/components/control/control", {
          id: "cols",
          label: "Max columns",
          min: 1,
          max: 6,
          step: 1,
          value: 4
        }) %>

        <%- include("/components/control/control", {
          id: "min",
          label: "Min width",
          min: 160,
          max: 480,
          step: 10,
          value: 220,
          unit: "px"
        }) %>

        <%- include("/components/control/control", {
          id: "gap",
          label: "Gap",
          min: 0,
          max: 48,
          step: 2,
          value: 16,
          unit: "px"
        }) %>

        <%- include("/components/control/control", {
          id: "width",
          label: "Container",
          min: 240,
          max: 1100,
          step: 1,
          value: 1100,
          unit: "px",
          sliderLabel: "Container width",
          numberMax: null
        }) %>

        <div class="control control--switches">
          <label class="switch">
            <input class="switch__input" type="checkbox" id="subgrid" checked>
            <span class="switch__label">Use subgrid</span>
          </label>
          <label class="switch">
            <input class="switch__input" type="checkbox" id="show-rows">
            <span class="switch__label">Show rows</span>
          </label>
          <label class="switch">
            <input class="switch__input" type="checkbox" id="containers">
            <span class="switch__label">Cells are containers</span>
          </label>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="stage stage--cards" aria-labelledby="cards-title">
        <div class="stage__bar">
          <h2 class="stage__heading" id="cards-title">Rows: line up the parts of each card</h2>
          <span class="stage__hint">Click a title or text to edit · drag the corner ↘ to resize</span>
        </div>
        <p class="stage__check" id="cards-check" role="status"></p>
        <div class="frame" id="frame">
          <div class="demo-grid sub-grid" id="cards" data-subgrid="true" data-show-rows="false" data-containers="false"></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="subgrid-info">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__head">How it works</div>
          <ol class="subgrid-info__steps">
            <li>Each card <strong>spans 4 rows</strong> of the grid: image, title, text, price.</li>
            <li><code>grid-template-rows: subgrid</code> makes the card use those <strong>shared rows</strong> instead of making its own.</li>
            <li>So the <strong>tallest</strong> title in a row sets that row's height, and every card's text and price start on the same line.</li>
            <li>Each <code>Cell</code> sits between the grid and the card, so it needs the same lines too.</li>
            <li><strong>The catch:</strong> a container (<code>container-type</code>) can't be a subgrid, and <code>Cell</code> is a container by default. Subgrid cards need <code>&lt;Cell cellNormal&gt;</code>, and their content can't use container queries. Try the <strong>Cells are containers</strong> switch.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__head">
            <span class="card__title">CSS</span>
            <button class="card__button" type="button" data-copy="cards-code">Copy</button>
          </div>
          <pre class="card__code"><code id="cards-code"></code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__head">
            React
            <button class="card__button" type="button" data-copy="react-code">Copy</button>
          </div>
          <pre class="card__code"><code id="react-code"></code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="stage stage--form" aria-labelledby="form-title">
        <div class="stage__bar">
          <h2 class="stage__heading" id="form-title">Columns: line up labels in a form</h2>
          <label class="switch">
            <input class="switch__input" type="checkbox" id="form-subgrid" checked>
            <span class="switch__label">Use subgrid</span>
          </label>
        </div>
        <p class="stage__explain">
          Subgrid works for columns too. Each field is its own row of label, input and hint. Without subgrid, every row
          sizes its label to fit, so the inputs start at different places. With <code>grid-template-columns: subgrid</code>,
          all fields share the form's columns: the <strong>longest label</strong> sets the width, and every input lines up.
        </p>
        <p class="stage__check" id="form-check" role="status"></p>
        <form class="form-demo" id="form" data-subgrid="true">
          <div class="form-demo__field">
            <label class="form-demo__label" for="f-name">Name</label>
            <input class="form-demo__input" id="f-name" type="text" placeholder="Alex Martin" autocomplete="off">
            <span class="form-demo__hint">As on your passport</span>
          </div>
          <div class="form-demo__field">
            <label class="form-demo__label" for="f-email">Email address</label>
            <input class="form-demo__input" id="f-email" type="email" placeholder="alex@example.com" autocomplete="off">
            <span class="form-demo__hint">For your tickets</span>
          </div>
          <div class="form-demo__field">
            <label class="form-demo__label" for="f-city">Departure city</label>
            <input class="form-demo__input" id="f-city" type="text" placeholder="Toronto" autocomplete="off">
            <span class="form-demo__hint">Airport or city</span>
          </div>
          <div class="form-demo__field">
            <label class="form-demo__label" for="f-travellers">Number of travellers</label>
            <input class="form-demo__input" id="f-travellers" type="number" min="1" max="9" value="2">
            <span class="form-demo__hint">Up to 9</span>
          </div>
        </form>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__head">
            CSS
            <button class="card__button" type="button" data-copy="form-code">Copy</button>
          </div>
          <pre class="card__code"><code id="form-code">.form {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr max-content;
  gap: 10px 12px;
}

.form > .field {                    /* label, input, hint */
  display: grid;
  grid-column: 1 / -1;              /* span every column */
  grid-template-columns: subgrid;   /* share the form's columns */
}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

<%- include("/partials/footer", {
  features: [
    {
      feature: "subgrid",
      test: "grid-template-rows: subgrid",
      caniuse: "subgrid",
      mdn: "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Grid_layout/Subgrid"
    },
    {
      feature: "grid",
      label: "CSS Grid",
      test: "display: grid",
      caniuse: "css-grid",
      mdn: "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/grid-template-columns"
    },
  ],
}) %>
